how to deal with self-doubt so I got a  great question for my youtube viewers  love you guys  andrew who wrote insane is got a young  friend Lee's got a young startup it's  not taking off for him he's starting to  question himself he's starting to wonder  you know do I have the entrepreneurial  Drive can I actually do this and he  wanted my advice on what to do next so  Andrew have two bits of advice to you  one it's totally normal and to remember  your why so the first point it's totally  normal  this is normal every entrepreneur goes  through this multiple times we like to  put our best foot forward we like people  to see only the positive side of us but  every entrepreneur at some point usually  multiple times thinks about quitting you  never hear about it nobody talks about  it you don't go to a networking event  and somebody comes up to you and says hi  I'm John yeah I don't know if I'm gonna  keep doing my business or not because  it's not taking off and I'm really  doubting myself right that never happens  but in reality everybody at some point  will be doubting themselves so  understand that it's normal and that's  totally okay which brings me to number  two remember your why you have to have a  strong enough why to get you through  this this is where a lot of  entrepreneurs fail they don't have a  strong enough why they jumped into the  business because maybe they thought it  would make them a lot of extra money and  they weren't prepared for the failures  and the Smashing of your self-worth  starting the business is one of the  hardest things you will ever do in your  life and you have to have a powerful  enough Y to get you through it something  way more powerful than just the money so  let me tell you about two times in my  life where I thought about quitting my  entrepreneurial dream the first was with  my first company where I was making $300  a month and wasn't able to survive and I  told my partner I quit and and you know  cried that night and the next day I woke  up and I went back to work with him and  what helped me through that was you know  I wanted to do something important and I  wanted to do something with that team  and I felt like I was putting up too  soon and and I would regret it that was  really my important why I loved what we  were doing I loved the people I was  working with and I felt like if I look  back in my life  I was 70 years old and I actually quit  there that I would regret it and I  wasn't making any money right I was I  was making $300 a month and could barely  survive and that's what got me through  that was what my important why was and  that that led us to be able to continue  to push on the second one is when I  started helping entrepreneurs I went to  do a presentation I was looking for a  new business model it sold my company I  was looking for a new thing to do with  my life and I was asked to do this  presentation at the YMCA  and we had done all this promotion of it  and only three people showed up for that  event and and it just killed me because  I put all of this time and effort and  value in and it just made me feel like  how am I ever gonna make a business out  of this how am I ever gonna be  successful when I can only get three  people to come to a free event but I did  that event I made the presentation and I  know that I touched those three people  who came out to see me  and when I walked away from that I knew  I had to continue to find a way to do it  I didn't know how I was gonna work out I  didn't know what the path was gonna be  but I knew that I loved it so much that  I had to find a way to continue doing  that and that was 12 13 years ago and  there's been so many ups and downs along  the way but my love for helping  entrepreneurs continues to burn bright  and makes you want to continue doing  this now it's taken the form of YouTube  videos I never would have thought that I  would be here doing this when I look  forward from where I was before but I  trusted that things would work out  because I was doing work that I loved  and that was my strong why to keep going  so you're going to be tested multiple  times in your career as an entrepreneur  and it's really going to come down to  how strong is that why and is it  powerful enough to keep you motivated to  keep going look at any entrepreneur and  look at their success story and look at  all the failures that they had to  overcome and not path the success most  people never make it because most people  quit and they give up too soon so find  your why make it powerful and believe in  your dream all the way believe for those  you watching I'd love to know what your  why is leave it in the comments below  and I'll be joining in the discussion  and if you like this video you want to  see more don't forget to subscribe to  the channel thank you so much for  watching  I'll see you soon I'm Calvin Moya I'm a  singer-songwriter and regular  personality I subscribe to Eva's  newsletter a few years ago it has really  helped me the newsletter is very  informative and inspiring and it has  helped me throughout my career so I  encourage you to don't give up you can  make it  subscribe to Evans newsletter today you  won't regret it  you
 

